# Line endings are load-bearing here, so they are not left to whatever a
# clone's `core.autocrlf` happens to be.
#
# EO hashes its own shipped role prompts to tell "EO wrote this" from "a
# person edited it" (SHIPPED_PROMPT_HASHES in src/main/roles/prompts.ts).
# The hash is over the file's bytes, so a CRLF checkout matches none of
# them: every shipped prompt would read as hand-edited, and `syncRolePrompts`
# would refuse to update any of them. That is a shipped-app bug on Windows,
# not only a test one — the prompts go into the installer as they sit on
# disk.
*         text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched, whatever the contents happen to look like to git's
# heuristic.
*.png     binary
*.ico     binary
*.icns    binary
*.svg     text eol=lf
*.snap    text eol=lf
